{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962539-werewolf-fertility-clinics-and-sperm-donation","id":962539,"title":"Werewolf Fertility Clinics and Sperm Donation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-02T15:43:45-07:00","id":962539,"title":"Werewolf Fertility Clinics and Sperm Donation","content":"So, I was just wondering if anyone had ever used fertility clinics or sperm donation for producing Garou? Since a Garou has a ten percent chance of producing Garou children (and a 90% chance of producing Garou Kinfolk) when they mate with normal human beings, it would make since for the Glass Walkers to start taking over fertility clinics and using Garou sperm for 10% of the women who are purchasing their services. Around 64,000 babies are born through IVF in the USA each year now so, if the Glass Walkers were able to gain control of 10% of the fertility clinics in the USA, they could produce 64 Garou children and 576 Garou Kinfolk every year (the current Garou population of the USA is estimated at ~640, ~1:500,000, so an extra 64 Garou per year would be a population explosion).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T16:04:48-07:00","id":962546,"title":"","content":"No. As an ST, I'd be unlikely to allow this to actually work. It smacks too much of the Weaver. Lots of flavor text reason you can give for why it fails. However, I would be willing to include this as some kind of plot point where DNA or some other faction tries to artificially create Garou this way. Or perhaps have some Glass Walker mad scientist try to figure out why it isn't able to work and perhaps create some kind of unique or ultra-rare event when it does work. I think there would be good stories to come out of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T16:47:56-07:00","id":962567,"title":"","content":"I doubt it is the sperm specifically or something so simple as genetics that leads to it. So really it should be the act itself that's important.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand why all Wolves aren't kinfolk is a bigger question..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T16:52:33-07:00","id":962570,"title":"","content":"It may just be me, but sometimes I think there is an overemphasis on running numbers....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T16:58:09-07:00","id":962571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962539-werewolf-fertility-clinics-and-sperm-donation?p=962570#post962570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may just be me, but sometimes I think there is an overemphasis on running numbers....</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> Especially for Werewolf where logic and science go out the window in favor of the reason &quot;because spirits say so&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T17:23:04-07:00","id":962583,"title":"","content":"Even getting away from the numbers focus, I do think it would make sense for there to be some Glass Walkers working in fertility. The &quot;It's too Weaver&quot; aspect goes out the window once we're talking about the most Weaver-happy Tribe. Of course, taking over enough clinics and getting lots of Garou sperm in the system (keeping in mind that there's little good data on how many children are born from donor gametes, a lot of IVF uses the gametes of two people that can't conceive naturally rather than donor sperm/eggs) is a pretty unlikely scenario to lead to reliable Garou births.<br /> <br /> It really should be a big &quot;thing&quot; but there's no reason why it might not be a major deal in a specific city with a lot of GW influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T17:44:34-07:00","id":962596,"title":"","content":"How would you run such a story? There might be 50 Glass Walkers in the USA, with 20 of them being fertile homid males, so they would have to convince twenty werewolves to contribute to their program. They might be able to convince the Children of Gaia and the Shadow Lords to contribute every month (though I would love to be a fly on the wall for that conversation), but I am not sure that they could get anyone else that they wanted to contribute. The Bone Gnawers might be willing to contribute, but the Glass Walkers would probably not accept their contributions. The Black Furies would be unable to contribute, Silver Fangs would be too proud, the Red Talons would be repulsed by the entire idea, and the Stargazers would think that it was too crass. Of the rest, I am not sure. What do you all think?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T21:09:07-07:00","id":962678,"title":"","content":"I wonder if there may be some spirtual reason that this couldn't be done. Garou aren't purely physical creatures, they are beings of spirit and flesh. Perhaps there are limited spiritual resources to empower the large number of Garou such activities could produce. Alternatively, maybe such large numbers of garou offspring couldn't be raised effectively and could cause chaos for future generations. Those are just my own speculations though, I don't recall anything mentioned in any book that would prevent this method from being highly effective and the Glass Walkers would certainly be willing to do it along with some other Tribes. Black Spiral Dancers would do it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 09-03-2016, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T22:12:57-07:00","id":962703,"title":"","content":"Your baseline population estimate for North America is demonstrably too low (e.g. there are 52 Glass Walkers in the New York region alone, another fifteen in the notoriously un-urban Southeast Appalachian range, with ~150 - ~200 of all tribes in that region. Based on figures released in 2002's ST Handbook, there is roughly one garou to every 500,000 humans and 30% of those Garou are in North America. Etc.) If we're going to do numbers, we need to at least do them right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T22:21:18-07:00","id":962704,"title":"","content":"Well, in that case, the number of Garou in North America would be ~4,500, which would make them less than 1:100,000 of the North American population, which would make them much more common than I thought. Can you give me a page number for the North American numbers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T22:26:45-07:00","id":962705,"title":"","content":"Page 33 or so has the breakdown.The same book also explains that there is no Garou gene and the creation of a Garou is largely a spiritual concern. Even without that source, the numbers remain demonstrably too low.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T22:39:44-07:00","id":962710,"title":"","content":"Where? I am seeing nothing about there not being a Garou gene or about any population numbers. Can you specific a heading under which I can find them? Not that it terribly matters, the fertility clinic scheme is not limited by lack of Garou but lack of human women.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T22:48:53-07:00","id":962712,"title":"","content":"Page 33 details the population figure of 1:500,000 and it's breakdown into various areas of the globe. Make sure you're looking at the 2002 Storyteller's Handbook. I'll quote it verbatim.<br /> <br /> &quot;Overall, there is about one Garou per 500,000 people in areas relatively hospitable to werewolves.&quot; Earlier on the same page, &quot;North America, Europe and Asia each host about one-third of the<br /> world\u2019s Garou, with the remaining ten percent spread through South America, Africa and Australia.&quot; The repudiation of the Garou gene is on page 20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T23:39:24-07:00","id":962729,"title":"","content":"The population numbers in the early Rage books are very suspect. To get all the Garou listed in Rage Across New York, which is where the 52 Glass walkers in New York are from, it is more like 1 Garou per 50,000 people. Australia has a similar ratio. Vancouver has even more Garou than that ratio. It is a far cry from the one per 500,000 listed afterwards. <br /> <br /> If we use that later ratio, the early Rage books are off by a factor of ten. Even if we take into consideration the Garou ratio is only generalized, and does not reflect local population (I can easily imagine low populated wilderness ratios in Yukon and elsewhere to have far more Garou than the human population would indicate, meaning higher populated areas would likely have less Garou) then Rage Across New York and other early books are still way, way off. <br /> <br /> If we take the 500,000 ratio seriously, it is hard to defend Rage Across New York whose 321 Garou (not counting any Black Spiral Dancers) reflects a population of around 160 million. New York's actual population is just under 20 million, and the entire United States is 320 million. That would mean half of the entire Garou expected in the US is in the New York area. If we used the one per 500,000 ratio, we'd expect the total Garou population to be around 40. Even if we add some of the population of the surrounding areas and decide that there is a higher presence of Garou in the area for whatever reason, we would fall very short of the canonical numbers.<br /> <br /> Dark Alliance: Vancouver lists 368 Garou. Rage Across Appalachia has less firm numbers, but is probably around 160. So in those three books alone, there are some 850 Garou. If we use the 500,000 number, that is more than the entire Garou population should be for Canada and the United States and almost as much as you would expect by adding Mexico. That would mean the rest of North America has almost no Garou.<br /> <br /> This is one reason I only use canon for inspiration instead of treating it like the law. Even if we try a &quot;No-Prize&quot; style solution and explain how it isn't really wrong, it just does not make any sense. The populations listed in the Rage books and the later statement of the human:Garou ratio are just incompatible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T08:08:48-07:00","id":962829,"title":"","content":"The Garou populations should follow the lupine populations. If we look at the gray wolf populations, 10% are found in Europe, 30% are found in North America, and 60% are found in Asia (primarily China, Far East Russia, Kazakhstan, and Mongolia), so it would make sense to have 30% of the Garou population in North America (what would have effectively happened during the colonization of North America is that the European Garou stole wolf kinfolk and human kinfolk from the three North American tribes). That is assuming, however, that Garou populations are linked to gray wolf population.<br /> <br /> It is probably wrong to only look at gray wolf populations however, since Garou are known to breed with every member of canis closely related to the gray wolf except for Coyote (which could be considered to be a lost tribe of Garou that was 'cursed' to be without Rage) and Dogs (which are too domesticated). Of the remaining species of canis, the African golden wolf and the golden jackal are the only ones that have been mentioned in the books that have sufficient population to be worth discussing. The African golden wolf, for example, is thought to have a population of around 200,000. The golden jackal (which is found throughout South Asia and Southeast Europe) is thought to have a population of around 200,000. Black backed jackals and side stripped jackals are too distantly related to the gray wolf to support Garou populations without Mokole assistance.<br /> <br /> So, if we consider the three populations of canines (African golden wolf, golden jackal, and gray wolf), the Garou population should be larger and/or more distributed because their population canis kinfolk have a combined population of 600,000 and are distributed across four continents. The Garou populations should be 3.4% Europe, 10% North America, 33.3% Africa, and 53.3% Asia. I would say that the African golden wolf and the golden jackal Garou are primarily going to primarily belong to the Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia, Glass Walkers, Red Talons, and Silent Striders Tribes. <br /> <br /> Of course, an interesting scenario would involve the gray wolf Garou deliberately ignoring the existence of the African golden wolf and golden jackal Garou populations out of racism (both human and wolf racism). Since the three groups of Garou would have always had equal populations, the gray wolf Garou could not have exterminated them like they did the Bunyip. In this case, there could be three times as many Garou as the official numbers, because the official numbers only include gray wolf Garou, but the gray wolf Garou refuse to work with their 'inferior' cousins because their 'inferior' cousins do not acknowledge their right to rule.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T08:22:56-07:00","id":962833,"title":"","content":"So just going by the ST Handbook, you have to keep in mind that the 1:500,000 number is an almost completely useless ratio. Never factor it in when trying to get <i>local</i> Garou population numbers since it's a worldwide number. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5307_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5307\" data-vbnamecard=\"5307\">loomer</a> points out, the book goes on to state that 30% of Garou are in North America. So Worldwide, there should currently be about 14,800 Garou. That means there are 4,440 in North America. From there, you have to decide how the tirbal numbers break down. But in any case, there are a lot more Garou in America than the 1:500,000 number indicates. And that is seemingly on purpose.<br /> <br /> Moving away from what is directly stated in the books, I say that the Glasswalkers make up 8-10% of the Garou nation, putting around 355-444 of them in North America. That is far more than the proposed 50 in the US alone.<br /> <br /> I agree that any numbers from early books are suspect. The writers, especially early on, didn't seem to know how numbers and ratios work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T08:30:14-07:00","id":962834,"title":"","content":"Funny you mention moving away from what's directly stated. In my files, approximately 8% of all garou entries that have their tribe as a known factor are Glass Walkers. You're spot on with the proportionate representation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T09:38:15-07:00","id":962852,"title":"","content":"Wow Asia is freakishly underpopulated by Garou(Africa and Australia don't have wolves natively) If it has 1/3 of the garou population but 4/7s of the human population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T10:40:52-07:00","id":962881,"title":"","content":"Asia also possesses 60% of the gray wolf population and 53% of the canis population, so the lack of Garou is even more extraordinary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T14:49:17-07:00","id":962974,"title":"","content":"Blame the Year of the Lotus...and White Wolf's desire to make large sections of Asia &quot;exotic&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T15:33:48-07:00","id":962985,"title":"","content":"I blame it more on people not getting over half the world's population is in Asia, or fundimentally how tiny Europe is both geographically and populationwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T16:28:40-07:00","id":962995,"title":"","content":"Or that over half of the population of the Earth has always been in Asia. There are still people that claim that half of the people alive in 100 AD were part of the Roman Empire, which is absurd considering that there were equivalent populations in each of China and India. Europe really was not that important until the 16th century, when they stole two continents and committed genocide against the native populations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T17:03:58-07:00","id":963003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962539-werewolf-fertility-clinics-and-sperm-donation?p=962995#post962995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or that over half of the population of the Earth has always been in Asia. There are still people that claim that half of the people alive in 100 AD were part of the Roman Empire, which is absurd considering that there were equivalent populations in each of China and India. Europe really was not that important until the 16th century, when they stole two continents and committed genocide against the native populations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, those nasty Europeans really have a lock on stuff like conquering and human misery. Not like the Mongols or the Aztecs or various other human groups have been acting like pricks towards each other since the dawn of time... European colonialism is just relatively recent and hilariously vogue to bitch about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T17:13:12-07:00","id":963007,"title":"","content":"Of course I don't think these numbers are being anything but ignored in w20 writeups. Cbs are presented as more playable. and shattered Dreams previews seemed to make the war of rage much less 1 sided..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T18:35:51-07:00","id":963029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962539-werewolf-fertility-clinics-and-sperm-donation?p=962974#post962974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blame the Year of the Lotus...and White Wolf's desire to make large sections of Asia &quot;exotic&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hengeyokai was actually more reasonable about this than a lot of later books. It at least noted that there were large quantities of the more &quot;common&quot; Garou tribes like Bone Gnawers and CoG that lived in the territory claimed by the Beast Courts and commonly joined in. Then Blood and Silk ruined everything with Hakken this, Hakken that, Hakken as the only tribe in the Beast Courts and coming to Japan later. Yet another reason to despise it, heaped on what is quite possibly the worst sidebar on Chinese Romanization in a White Wolf book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T18:42:02-07:00","id":963033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962539-werewolf-fertility-clinics-and-sperm-donation?p=963029#post963029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hengeyokai was actually more reasonable about this than a lot of later books. It at least noted that there were large quantities of the more &quot;common&quot; Garou tribes like Bone Gnawers and CoG that lived in the territory claimed by the Beast Courts and commonly joined in. Then Blood and Silk ruined everything with Hakken this, Hakken that, Hakken as the only tribe in the Beast Courts and coming to Japan later. Yet another reason to despise it, heaped on what is quite possibly the worst sidebar on Chinese Romanization in a White Wolf book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The thing is the Beast courts are objectively better at their job and Gaia intention. So situations where the option exists they will slowly come to domnate.. See the Adhi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T19:26:43-07:00","id":963046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962539-werewolf-fertility-clinics-and-sperm-donation?p=963029#post963029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hengeyokai was actually more reasonable about this than a lot of later books. It at least noted that there were large quantities of the more &quot;common&quot; Garou tribes like Bone Gnawers and CoG that lived in the territory claimed by the Beast Courts and commonly joined in. Then Blood and Silk ruined everything with Hakken this, Hakken that, Hakken as the only tribe in the Beast Courts and coming to Japan later. Yet another reason to despise it, heaped on what is quite possibly the worst sidebar on Chinese Romanization in a White Wolf book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I never minded the idea of the courts (much like I do like the Ahadi), I just was never a fan of how things were executed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T21:29:18-07:00","id":963087,"title":"","content":"I thought that the Courts should have used the Kinfolk more, as they could have been involved in administrative and service positions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T09:42:16-07:00","id":963252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962539-werewolf-fertility-clinics-and-sperm-donation?p=963046#post963046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I never minded the idea of the courts (much like I do like the Ahadi), I just was never a fan of how things were executed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that there's no COG Asian off shoot has always bugged me... but we've already had a thread on this. And maybe Hakken as a true tribe under some sort of Samurai totem.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T10:10:01-07:00","id":963259,"title":"","content":"I think that all of the European Tribes should have had Asian versions. After all, the Celts and Germans invaded and conquered areas throughout Asia, so I imagine that their Garou relatives would have followed. Heck, they just found the remains of a Celtic settlement in Xinjiang, China just ten years ago (<a href=\"http://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/asia/a-meeting-of-civilisations-the-mystery-of-chinas-celtic-mummies-5330366.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.independent.co.uk/news/wo...s-5330366.html</a>), so it would not be unreasonable to have Chinese Fianna running around Xinjiang.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T10:18:21-07:00","id":963261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962539-werewolf-fertility-clinics-and-sperm-donation#post962539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I was just wondering if anyone had ever used fertility clinics or sperm donation for producing Garou? Since a Garou has a ten percent chance of producing Garou children (and a 90% chance of producing Garou Kinfolk) when they mate with normal human beings, it would make since for the Glass Walkers to start taking over fertility clinics and using Garou sperm for 10% of the women who are purchasing their services.</div> </div> </div> </div>When they mate with normal human beings, Garou cannot produce Garou. Garou are only born from mating with Kinfolk or other Garou. Now, a Glass Walker clinic could totally try and match people up based on their spiritual heritage and try and encourage Kin-Kin or Kin-Garou IVF matches, which would totally be in line with the Garou having killed the Apis, Gaia's matchmakers. Now whether this upsets Gaia or Minotaur, that would be up to the GM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T10:37:28-07:00","id":963265,"title":"","content":"No, I think that is incorrect. When you look under the description of the breeds (Werewolf (Revised), p. 59), it says &quot;What determines breed? Simply enough, it's the natural form of the werewolf's mother, whether she's Kinfolk, Garou, ordinary human or wolf.&quot; So Garou can explicitly be born from non-Kinfolk humans and non-Kinfolk wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 09-04-2016, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T11:42:21-07:00","id":963305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962539-werewolf-fertility-clinics-and-sperm-donation?p=963259#post963259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that all of the European Tribes should have had Asian versions. After all, the Celts and Germans invaded and conquered areas throughout Asia, so I imagine that their Garou relatives would have followed. Heck, they just found the remains of a Celtic settlement in Xinjiang, China just ten years ago (<a href=\"http://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/asia/a-meeting-of-civilisations-the-mystery-of-chinas-celtic-mummies-5330366.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.independent.co.uk/news/wo...s-5330366.html</a>), so it would not be unreasonable to have Chinese Fianna running around Xinjiang.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really? I mean Garou don't tend to stick around when their relatives die out. Yes there were conquests in the past, but the Mongols pushed into Poland you don't see that as an argument for Polish Khan or Kitsune.<br /> <br /> Of the tribes I would thinking<br /> <br /> Red talons: They are too wolfy while they might have a place in Asia between it poaching on Stargazer kin and their inability to think human enough to get along with other Fera I imagine there's been abit of a quiet push against them perhaps active genocide.<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs: the Mandate of Heaven does not mark the Tribe of the Falcon. I think perhaps their lack of push outside India has been the Kitsune.. doing their job. They seem to have been very much at the heart of the Garou nation and its failure to do as Gaia intended. The Kitsune have a job to bring down dynasties that have become a problem..<br /> <br /> Shadow Lords and Hakken: In my head canon both exist in the area and they do not get along. Hakken are more likely to join the Beast courts while Other Lords are more likely to direct themselves at garou only situations.<br /> <br /> Get of Fenris: Yes Vikings went everywhere, but the argument I made about Polish Kitsune should apply here.<br /> <br /> Black Furies: There are some strong matriarchal societies in Asia. On the other hand, they have strong ties to Greece and its patriarchy. The Greeks did ride to India and trade to China. But we have the same issues as with the Get, on the other hand they might trade Greek for the Matriarchies. I think perhaps there are some but not enough for it to matter on the Fera scene.<br /> <br /> Fianna: Similar arguments, I don't see a replacement kin for them.<br /> <br /> Bonegnawers: I think this is more an issue of being edged out. The boli seem to have qualities both of Glasswalkers and Bonegnawers. Pressures may have forced both tribes to combine and Glasswalkers came out on top. On the other hand there's plenty of room on the edges for things that are multigenerational feral dogs in asia...<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia: There really should be a whole Kirin variant Camp/Tribal offshoot dedicated to working with other Fera.<br /> <br /> Silent Striders: They wander. It is their nature. There are nomadic communties to take them up in Asia though such a life style can't be good for breeding in general.<br /> <br /> Uktena: Not a European Tribe but I'm going to talk about them. They were still alive in Asia as of the Dark Ages among various repressed cultures like the Ainu and stronger groups like the Mongols. I don't see any reason why they wouldn't be involved in the Court except this being a retcon written after Hengeyokai.<br /> <br /> So I guess in sum I feel Uktena, and COG really should have more of a face in the Emerald Courts. While other tribes might have token connections or even somewhat extensive connections throughout Asia. This should also probably be the case with the Bastet, Bahgeera should be playing to the courts. And perhaps some Discussion on why the Qualmi aren't in Asia. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Come to think of it are Human bastet Kinfolk universal Kinfolk for bastet? That might explain why there aren't any Swara in India...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T11:48:48-07:00","id":963311,"title":"","content":"Glasswalkers and Bone Gnawers are explicitly mentioned in Hengeyokai as members of the Beast Courts. I think that the Human Kinfolk are specific to each Tribe, as are the Feline Kinfolk, though that may just be my own biases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T06:31:11-07:00","id":1481842,"title":"","content":"In Rage across Australia is mentioned a cloning of the Bunyip plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T08:14:05-07:00","id":1481843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962539-werewolf-fertility-clinics-and-sperm-donation?p=963305#post963305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really? I mean Garou don't tend to stick around when their relatives die out. Yes there were conquests in the past, but the Mongols pushed into Poland you don't see that as an argument for Polish Khan or Kitsune.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would 100% argue that there should be european and american kitsune(and that they shouldn't be called kitsune). There are massive fox populations on both continents And common mythology about fox shifters(especially in native tribes of north america like the inuit).<br /> <br /> Kitsune being asia exclusive is asian exotisism and cultural white-washing(or asia-washing I guess?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T09:05:25-07:00","id":1482001,"title":"","content":"It came up as a hypothetical with an ST I've been running with recently where he suggested that, should it actually work, putting a bunch of unknowing kinfolk or possible garou out in the world via sperm donation would help hunters and spirals at least as much as it helps the donating gaian garou. Even glasswalker recordkeeping isn't perfect and you aren't going to be able to put a kinfetch on every relevant infant just in case garou gametes were used.<br /> <br /> Also what BlackFox said about Magadon or Shinzui or other malefactors, should they catch wind, using the garou donors' DNA for their own shenanigans. In the best case, unable to do anything more devastating using it to make assassination virus or tracking algorithms, in the worst case, able to do some proper Shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","user":"Devidramoth","date":". 05-26-2022, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T08:57:21-07:00","id":1482075,"title":"","content":"I used to run a story centered on BSD using fertility clinic described in Freak Legion (for producing fomori). The same idea was used in first &quot;When will you rage&quot; (story about Samuel Haight) My conclusion? It is entirely possible BUT:<br /> 1. You have to track every woman in which you put a potential Garou and that would be hard<br /> 2. Explain them that (in case of First Change happening) you take over their child.<br /> 3. Try to avoid them suing you for leaking of the data (because how a Garou would know about the origin of this child)<br /> 4. In case of the early symptoms of the First Change (and I believe that most of the clinic's clients are ordinary human females/couples, in other case it would be useless) most of the kids would end in the mental health institiutions and that would propably means Magadon sedatives.<br /> 4. I think that, even if Pentex and all its subsidiaries are unknown to most Garou, most of them can sense something weird around its products and can warn their kinfolks. Humans (eg. clients) don't have that luxury and that means exposure on Wyrm products since early childhood for potential Garou. Not to mention that Banes can alert BSD of potential Garou. <br /> 5. What if some BSD wants to donate?<br /> 6. What if some other supernatural creature would like to use your clinic (Giovanni trying to create Rosselini revenants).<br /> 7. Most likely a Garou created that way would be Weaver tainted (causing mistrust in most septs) or worse Wyrm tainted (as Magadon produce many things you would use in that clinic).<br /> So basically I think it's possible. The question is what for? And would the costs be acceptable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 05-28-2022, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T09:38:58-07:00","id":1482165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962539-werewolf-fertility-clinics-and-sperm-donation?p=1482075#post1482075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used to run a story centered on BSD using fertility clinic described in Freak Legion (for producing fomori). The same idea was used in first &quot;When will you rage&quot; (story about Samuel Haight) My conclusion? It is entirely possible BUT:<br /> 1. You have to track every woman in which you put a potential Garou and that would be hard<br /> 2. Explain them that (in case of First Change happening) you take over their child.<br /> 3. Try to avoid them suing you for leaking of the data (because how a Garou would know about the origin of this child)<br /> ...<br /> 5. What if some BSD wants to donate?<br /> 6. What if some other supernatural creature would like to use your clinic (Giovanni tried to create Rosselini revenants).<br /> ...<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I mean, if it is BSDs running the clinic I have a hard time seeing them being overly concerned about the privacy or consent of the mothers and children using their clinic, unless I've badly misunderstood the ethics of the spiral.<br /> <br /> Revenants are the combined efforts of of some of the most sorcerously inclined children of Enoch, who believed in adaptation and evolution before those concepts even had names, working continuously, alongside mages, for literal millennia with a mastery over spirit and flesh that far exceeds even modern medicine. It's akin to breeding two mules together to make thoroghbread cold-blood horse. I don't see it as something that can be 'automated' to happen with only mundane medicine overseeing the process.<br /> <br /> Even if the Giovanni were to be more hands on, I imagine most human clients would notice the 5 to 10 year long pregnancy and constant cravings for blood and get a little suspicious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T11:33:28-07:00","id":1482182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Devidramoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962539-werewolf-fertility-clinics-and-sperm-donation?p=1482165#post1482165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revenants are the combined efforts of of some of the most sorcerously inclined children of Enoch, who believed in adaptation and evolution before those concepts even had names, working continuously, alongside mages, for literal millennia with a mastery over spirit and flesh that far exceeds even modern medicine. It's akin to breeding two mules together to make thoroghbread cold-blood horse. I don't see it as something that can be 'automated' to happen with only mundane medicine overseeing the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original 4 Tzimisce Revenant families were products of magic, but others have cropped up with different origins since then(in mage terms, the mythic thread has been planted, making it orders of magnitude easier for others to follow). Revenant families can also result from Dhampir's breeding with mortals as per Kindred of the ebony kingdom.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Devidramoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962539-werewolf-fertility-clinics-and-sperm-donation?p=1482165#post1482165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if the Giovanni were to be more hands on, I imagine most human clients would notice the 5 to 10 year long pregnancy and constant cravings for blood and get a little suspicious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nowhere Near that long, but they actually outline the revenant creation rituals in Mind's Eye and they require the mother have some form of vampire blood in their system(so it's Ghoul/revenant exclusive). The only people the Giovanni would be able grow revenants from would be blood-bonded anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T13:46:47-07:00","id":1482193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Devidramoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962539-werewolf-fertility-clinics-and-sperm-donation?p=1482165#post1482165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if it is BSDs running the clinic I have a hard time seeing them being overly concerned about the privacy or consent of the mothers and children using their clinic, unless I've badly misunderstood the ethics of the spiral.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, but we were talking about a clinic run by Glass Walkers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Devidramoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962539-werewolf-fertility-clinics-and-sperm-donation?p=1482165#post1482165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revenants are the combined efforts of of some of the most sorcerously inclined children of Enoch, who believed in adaptation and evolution before those concepts even had names, working continuously, alongside mages, for literal millennia with a mastery over spirit and flesh that far exceeds even modern medicine. It's akin to breeding two mules together to make thoroghbread cold-blood horse. I don't see it as something that can be 'automated' to happen with only mundane medicine overseeing the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. But who will forbid them to try? As for Rossellini family (Giovanni Revenants) they were introduced into the clan in XVI century and show (at least some of them) as Revenants in V20. So it's not millenia but 5 centuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":